ew-england-patriots","type":"BlogEntry","byline":"Mike Reiss","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"As J.C. Jackson heads to free agency, what's next for Patriots at cornerback?","description":"The Patriots, who seem likely to lose their promising ball hawk, can explore potential replacements in free agency and the 2022 NFL draft.","published":"2022-03-09T12:35:52.000+00:00","url":"http://espn.com/blog/new-england-patriots/post/_/id/4824975/as-j-c-jackson-heads-to-free-agency-whats-next-for-patriots-at-cornerback","type":"BlogEntry","byline":"Mike Reiss","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Sticking with Cam Newton gives Bill Belichick cover for Patriots' roster issues","description":"The QB's running helps New England hide personnel problems at tight end and receiver that would be more exposed by a traditional pocket passer.","published":"2020-12-13T17:52:27.000+00:00","url":"http://espn.com/blog/new-england-patriots/post/_/id/4821796/sticking-with-cam-newton-gives-bill-belichick-cover-for-patriots-roster-issues","type":"BlogEntry","byline":"Mike Reiss","source":"ESPN"},{"headline":"Patriots run off the field by L.A. Rams as their playoff hopes fade","description":"The Patriots' feeble offense was subdued by the Rams, putting New England on the verge of missing the postseason for the first time since 2008.","published":"2020-12-11T15:51:02.000+00:00","url":"http://espn.com/blog/new-england-patriots/post/_/id/4821802/patriots-run-off-the-field-by-rams-as-their-playoff-hopes-fade-away","type":"BlogEntry","byline":"Mike Reiss","source":"ESPN"}],"wiki":{"title":"Myles Bryant","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Myles_Bryant","description":"American football player (born 1998)","touched":"2026-11-17T20:04:41Z","intro":"Myles Bryant (born January 2, 1998) is an American professional football defensive back for the Detroit Lions of the National Football League (NFL). He played college football for the Washington Huskies and was signed by the New England Patriots as an undrafted free agent following the 2020 NFL Draft.","sections":[{"key":"college","title":"College career","text":"Bryant played college football at Washington, where he was a three-time All-Pac-12 selection—twice on the second-team, and once as an honorable mention. He appeared in a total of 39 games, recording 177 tackles, 4 interceptions, 3 forced fumbles, and 3.5 sacks."},{"key":"career","title":"Professional career","text":"NEW ENGLAND PATRIOTS\nBryant went undrafted in the 2020 NFL draft, and signed with the New England Patriots on May 5, 2020. He was waived during final roster cuts on September 5, and re-signed to the team's practice squad the next day. He was promoted to the active roster on September 16, made his NFL debut in Week 8 against the Buffalo Bills,  recorded his first tackle two weeks later in a win against the Baltimore Ravens, and recorded his first interception in week 14 against the Los Angeles Rams.\nOn August 31, 2021, Bryant was waived by the Patriots and re-signed to the team's practice squad. He was promoted to the active roster on October 19. In the Patriots' 54–13 rout of the New York Jets, Bryant recorded his first sack and first forced fumble.\n\nHOUSTON TEXANS\nOn April 2, 2024, Bryant signed with the Houston Texans. He was promoted to the active roster on November 28.\nOn May 21, 2025, Bryant re-signed with the Texans. He was released on August 26 as part of final roster cuts, and re-signed to the practice squad. On November 12, Bryant was signed to the active roster.\n\nCLEVELAND BROWNS\nOn April 6, 2026, Bryant signed with the Cleveland Browns. On August 30, he was released by Cleveland as a part of final roster cuts; he was re-signed to the team's practice squad the following day. He was released on September 23 and re-signed to the practice squad five days later. On October 13, Bryant was released.\n\nDETROIT LIONS\nOn October 22, 2026, Bryant signed with the Detroit Lions practice squad."}],"wikidataId":"Q99523144","social":{}},"transactions":[{"date":"2026-10-22","text":"Signed WR DeAndre Carter to the active roster. Signed S Myles Bryant to the practice squad."}],"links":{"espn":"https://www.espn.com/nfl/player/_/id/4039010","pfr":"https://www.pro-football-reference.com/players/B/BryaMy01.htm","pff":"https://www.pff.com/nfl/players/myles-bryant/43336","otc":"https://overthecap.com/player/myles-bryant/9271","wikipedia":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Myles_Bryant"},"insights":["2026 cap number of $220K is the 67th-largest on the roster.","Contract expires after this season.","Entered the league in 2020 as an undrafted free agent."]}